[quote]
[center][size=3][color=#FFB833][b]📢 RELEASE NOTICE: v0.2.9 PULLED FORWARD FOR URGENT FIXES[/b][/color][/size][/center]
This release was [b]pulled forward ahead of schedule to deliver urgent fixes[/b] for signaling, double-track right-hand running, DM3/thermal physics, MU lighting, and AI worker stability. Because of this expedited release, [b]not all new features originally planned for 0.2.9 made it in[/b] — remaining Phase 2 worker features (including in-game UI selection for Multi-Stop Itineraries, Intermediate Tail-Cut Wagon Drop-Offs, Diegetic Station Paperwork / Itinerary Sheets, and full Autonomous Run-Around / Reverse Shoving) have been deferred to the next update.
[/quote]

[size=4][b][color=#55DD55]✦ Compatibility: Persistent Jobs is DEFINITELY Supported![/color][/b][/size]
[quote]
[b]Persistent Jobs is 100% officially supported and integrated into AI Traffic (v0.2.8+).[/b]
Even though the [i]Persistent Jobs[/i] mod page may currently claim that AI Traffic is unsupported or incompatible, [b]this is outdated[/b]. AI Traffic includes dedicated integration patches that reflect lightweight suspended cars ([i]FarCarOpt[/i]) in pathfinding, protect yard tracks, and segregate debt ledgers so both mods run together seamlessly!
[/quote]

[size=4][b][color=#FFB833]✦ What's New in Version 0.2.9[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Signaling Classification & Contention Storm Fixes:[/b] Fixed combined Main/Entry masts (e.g. OWC Entry Signal A), added world-load/toggle signal index invalidation with post-load rescans, fixed aspect display labels, and added a 5s failure cooldown to stop per-tick DVSignals reservation storms.
[*][b]Right-Hand Running & CW–OWC Routing Fixes:[/b] Separated 0.8m diamond crossings (0.35m merge threshold) from phantom degree-4 nodes, enabled safe same-direction following on paired right-hand double tracks, added proactive right-hand corridor realignment, prevented wrong-way parallel spawns, and fixed corridor token leaks.
[*][b]Destination Exit Signal & Two-Open-Sided Track Stopping:[/b] Arriving trains now detect and brake cleanly before destination exit signals and forward switches instead of rolling past into the throat.
[*][b]DM3 Gearbox, 65 km/h Cap & Thermal Protection:[/b] Fixed DM3 A2–B2 gear snap-back, froze hill-stagnation timers during DM3 shifts, capped DM3 speed at 65 km/h, added universal thermal throttle cut (>= 95°C) and dynamic brake thermal cutoff (> 90°C), and fixed false job completion on permanent hill stalls.
[*][b]MU Headlight Cross-Talk & Terminal Parked Latch:[/b] Stopped MU-connected trailing helper locomotives from extinguishing the lead locomotive's forward headlights at night, and eliminated per-frame reverser/headlight servo ping-pong on parked consists.
[*][b]AI Worker Cancellation Refunds & Multi-Stop Architecture [i](Multi-Stop Not Selectable In-Game Yet)[/i]:[/b] Added a 10s/25m 100% grace window and pro-rated mid-transit cancellation refunds for AI Workers. The underlying multi-stop itinerary & non-blocking waypoint departure system is implemented as backend architecture only and [b]cannot be selected in-game yet[/b] (in-game dispatch remains single A-to-B hauls until the next update).
[*][b]Valley-Wide Comms Radio Worker Channel:[/b] Monitor active worker trains remotely from anywhere on the map, issue in-flight orders ([i]Resume Run[/i], [i]Hold at Next Loop[/i], [i]Emergency Stop[/i]), and resolve 30s blocked-track alerts via the Escalation Menu.
[*][b]In-Cab Co-Pilot Touch-to-Yield & Destination Congestion Staging:[/b] Moving cab controls hands authority cleanly to the player (re-engage smoothly with [b]Ctrl+A[/b] or Comms Radio), caps slip/stall fuel/oil/sand burn, and safely holds workers outside occupied destination throats with Comms Radio warning pings.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#FFB833]✦ Core Features Overview[/color][/b][/size]

[b][color=#55DD55]1. Player-Employed AI Workers (Phase 2)[/color][/b]
[list]
[*][b]Point-to-Point Delivery:[/b] Hire AI engineers via the Comms Radio ([b]AI Worker[/b] mode) to haul assembled consists from Station A to Station B.
[*][b]Dynamic Clear Siding Auto-Selection:[/b] Evaluates receiving/yard tracks at destination for length and clearance before dispatch.
[*][b]Realistic Economy & Automation:[/b] Charges distance/tonnage wages, connects air hoses, releases handbrakes, starts engines, and returns 100% control upon arrival.
[/list]

[b][color=#55DD55]2. Autonomous AI Traffic & Signaling[/color][/b]
[list]
[*][b]Realistic Train Operations:[/b] Closed-loop PID throttle/brake regulation, speed profile calculations, Bezier curve evaluation, and powertrain thermal protection.
[*][b]DVSignals Interlocking:[/b] Respects physical German H/V signals, block reservations, player right-of-way, and single-track corridor tokens.
[*][b]Deadlock Immunity:[/b] Passing siding holds, dynamic alternate siding repathing, and safe 5-minute stuck-train despawn safeguards.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#FFB833]✦ Requirements & Installation[/color][/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*][b]Derail Valley[/b] (Latest Steam build) + [b]Unity Mod Manager (UMM)[/b] v0.27.0+
[*][b]DVSignals[/b] (Required for block reservations & signal aspects)
[*][b]CommsRadioAPI[/b] (Required for Comms Radio AI Worker mode)
[*][i]Double Track[/i] ([b]Strongly Recommended[/b] to minimize single-track bottlenecks)
[*][b]Persistent Jobs[/b] ([b]Fully Compatible & Supported![/b])
[/list]

[b]Install:[/b] Download [b]AITraffic-v0.2.9.zip[/b] and drop into UMM, or extract into [i]Derail Valley/Mods/[/i].
